\fs24 \cf0 Case counts! "buffalo nickel" will not find "Buffalo Nickel".\
\
You can use the UNIX wildcard  * (asterisk) -- any number of characters will be matched. For example, "Be*" would match "Beggars Banquet", "Better Living Through Chemistry", and "Beyond & Back". You can use the asterisk on either side or both sides of your string.\
\
If any results are found they will be displayed in a choose box:\
\
