\cf0 \
Notice that my iPod was also searched. If you have indexed your iPod with Spotlight you will get results from iPod. (You can index your iPod using the "mdutil" command or by using Kevin Wojniak's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.kainjow.com/software/"}}{\fldrslt Spodlight}}.)\
\
Select the files you want to add to iTunes and press "OK". For best results, I would suggest setting iTunes preferences to "Copy files to Music folder when adding to Library". This works nicely when copying files from iPod.\
\
\'a5 I have named the script using a leading "_" so that it appears close to the top in the iTunes Script Menu. You can rename the script if you wish.\
